<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zamboanga City</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zamboanga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zamboanga City is a port on the western tip of the Zamboanga Peninsula in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a>, in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> built Fort Pilar there in 1635 as its main stronghold against the Moro sultanates of Mindanao and Sulu. Its Christian population speaks Chavacano, a Spanish-based <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">creole</a> language.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zamboanga-city.jpg" alt="Zamboanga City" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ralff Nestor Nacor · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zamboanga_City_Hall_%26_Rizal_Park,_Mar_2026.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
